# Story page: tip
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Tail Tip
---
In the topsy-turvy mirrors, one reflection held something out: the very tip of a very long tail.

'Yours,' said the reflection. 'You will want it back eventually. Everyone does.'

{name} took it. It was warm, and it wriggled a little, as though glad to be home. Of all the things in this book, it is the one I would most like to forget.
